ent & Transformation Leadership Close About About About Overview About Widener Points of Pride Widener at a Glance Our Leadership Strategy, Mission & History Diversity, Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Community Resources Clinics & Centers Wolfgram Memorial Library Observatory Taylor Arboretum Faculty Directory Offices & Departments Maps & Directions Work at Widener President's Leadership Team Close Search Website AI Search Apply Visit Search Website AI Search Mega Nav Academics Find Your Program Explore All Programs Undergraduate Majors Graduate & Law Programs Adult & Continuing Studies Online Programs Colleges & Schools College of Arts & Sciences College of Health & Human Services School of Business Administration School of Engineering Dwyer School of Nursing Center for Continuing Studies Commonwealth Law School Delaware Law School Resources for Success Academic & Career Support Accessibility Co-Ops & Internships Study Away Wolfgram Library Academic Calendar Catalogs & Handbooks Faculty Directory Labs & Learning Spaces Academic Leadership Admissions & Aid Admissions Pathways Undergraduate Graduate Adult & Continuing Studies Transfer International Military & Veteran Tuition & Aid Undergraduate Graduate Adult & Continuing Studies Visit Campus Undergraduate Graduate Adult & Continuing Studies Apply Now Check Application Status Request Info Why Widener Career Inside Track Faculty Mentorship Research & Innovation Leadership Development Location Matters Student Stories Alumni Success Points of Pride Widener at a Glance Campus Life Our Campus Campus Vibe Where to Live Where to Eat What's Nearby Get Involved Clubs & Organizations Athletics & Club Sports Music & Performing Arts Fraternity & Sorority Life Well-Being Belonging Mental Health & Counseling Health & Fitness Personal & Community Safety Engage Widener mySuccess WidenerCONNECT Student Engagement & Transformation Leadership About About Widener Points of Pride Widener at a Glance Our Leadership Strategy, Mission & History Diversity, Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Community Resources Clinics & Centers Wolfgram Memorial Library Observatory Taylor Arboretum Faculty Directory Offices & Departments Maps & Directions Work at Widener President's Leadership Team Apply Visit Utility Menu WU Links myWidener mySuccess Canvas Outlook Email Office365 Zoom Self Service Wolfgram Library Campus Store Resources For You High School Students New First-Year & Transfer Students Current Students Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni Community & Partners News Events Athletics ♥ Give Faculty & Staff Helpful Resources Recent News New Business Dean Brings Fresh Ideas and a Vision for Student Success Widener has welcomed Cary Caro as dean of the School of Business Administration. We sat down with Caro to learn more about his background and his vision for the future of business education at Widener. Why We Give Back: Robin Dole and Joe Gelormini ’14 ‘23 Robin Dole and Joe Gelormini’s shared connection to Widener reflects a deep, ongoing commitment to the university’s growth and impact, from Robin’s decades of leadership as a faculty member and now dean, to Joe’s engagement as both an undergraduate and graduate alumnus. Together, they support efforts that expand hands-on learning opportunities and strengthen services for the surrounding community. Business Faculty Shine at Conference, Students Gain Hands-On Experience and Valuable Connections The School of Business Administration recently served as the host institution for the 55th annual conference of the Northeast Decision Sciences Institute. Widener was well represented throughout the event with students, faculty and staff participation. Noteworthy Updates Upcoming Events October 9 • 08:00 AM Homecoming (Oct. 9-10) Get Excited for Homecoming! Visit our alumni website for more details about this year's entire week September 9 • 11:00 AM Care Fair September 28 • 04:00 PM Dr. Brent's Queer History Mystery (9/28-10/23) View More Events Pride Personified \"Pride Personified\" is a celebration of the people who make the Widener community outstanding. Employees are invited to nominate their colleagues who exceed the highest expectations, and whose standards of excellence make the Widener community an even better place. Do you have a colleague who exceeds the highest expectations? Someone whose standard of excellence makes our Widener community an even better place? Nominate a Colleague Campus Resources Wolfgram Memorial Library The Wolfgram Memorial Library is open to Widener students, faculty and staff and is the home of all of your resource needs. Dining Widener offers a variety of dining and meal plan options to fit into a variety of lifestyles. Pride Recreation Center We offer numerous recreational opportunities and team activities to help you live healthy and stay active. Book A Room Widener offers an easy way for faculty and staff to reserve a room for a variety of purposes. Campus & Community Resources We're home to an elaborate network of campus and community resources. Bookstore The Widener Bookstore has everything from apparel to show off your pride to supplies to further your education. Academic Resources Academic Calendar The Widener University academic calendar shows key academic dates for all undergraduate, graduate, and adult and professional studies students. Academic Offices Our departments and offices offer help and support to all students in order to achieve success in their fields. Faculty Directory Our faculty understand that academic success is key and are always open to outreach from all students. Program Directory Our wide variety of programs offer something for both graduate and undergraduate students to achieve success in their field of interest. Catalogs Our catalogs offer both graduate and undergraduate students important information about programs, curricula, and courses. Get Connected Connect with Widener on social media! Facebook Instagram Twitter LinkedIn Important Contacts Human Resources Payroll Career Opportunities for Current Employees Information Technology Services Maintaining a safe, caring, and supportive community continues with you! Help keep our campus safe by reporting issues or concerns that may affect the well-being of a student or campus community member such as engaging in distressed or disruptive behaviors, sexual misconduct, or hazing. Our teams are equipped to respond to your concerns with helpful support, respect, and compassion. REPORT IT Need Additional Help? If you need assistance finding what you are looking for or would like to report an error, please contact web@widener.edu . For issues with your internet, email, or computer network set-up, please contact the ITS helpdesk . One University Place Chester, PA 19013 1-888-WIDENER Facebook Widener Instagram LinkedIn Widener TikTok Twitter Youtube Interactive Campus Map Apply to Widener Directions, Parking & Transportation Explore All Programs Work at Widener © 2026 Widener University Widener University uses IP2Location.io IP geolocation web service. Campus Safety Report It Privacy Consumer Information"
    },
