    "https://mysuccess.widener.edu/s/career-success": {
      "title": "My Career Success",
      "description": "My Career Success | Widener mySuccess Skip to main content Skip to main site navigation Skip to main content Blog Success Events myWidener mySuccess Menu Search My Toolkit New First-Year & Transfer Students Undergraduate Students Graduate & Online Students International Students My Academics Course Registration & Degree Planning Exploratory Studies Academic Support & Mentorship Tips for Academic Success Academic Tools & Resources Academic FAQs Math Center Writing Center My Experience Co-Ops, Internships & Student Jobs Civic Engagement Study & Intern Away Student Research Campus Clubs & Programs My Wellbeing Accessibility Belonging Financial Wellness Mental Health Personal Safety Physical Health Spiritual Wellness My Career Explore & Design My Career My Values, Strengths & Skills Career Prep Programs Professional Branding & Networking Job Search & Applications Resumes, Cover Letters & Portfolios Interviewing, Salary & Offer Negotiations Planning for Grad & Law School Career Growth & Transitions Our Success Success Stories Student News Blog Success Events myWidener Search My Career Success Whether you're looking for personalized support from Widener's Career Design and Development Office, career inspiration, skills-building and job-landing resources, or help designing a meaningful, profitable career—this is the place for all your career development needs. Turn Your Career Aspirations Into Reality Whether you're an undergraduate, graduate, or taking a non-traditional path, Widener University is here to guide you towards a fulfilling career and provide you with support and resources to build the skills and experiences to achieve your career goals. After all, it's not just about landing your first or next job—it's about setting you up for lifelong professional success. Resources & Guidance for Career Success Explore & Design My Career My Values, Strengths & Skills Career Prep Programs Professional Branding & Networking Job Search & Applications Career Growth & Transitions Resumes, Cover Letters, & Portfolios Interviewing, Salary & Offer Negotiations Graduate School Prep Receive Personalized, 1:1 Career Support & Expert Guidance The partnership you build with Design & Development Office's expert career counselors is an important one. They'll be your trusted ally, offering valuable insights, resources, and strategies to help you navigate your unique path to career success, including how to: Identify and connect your skills and interests to professional and personal aspirations, Find co-op and internship experiences to strengthen your resume before you graduate, Search, apply, and interview for jobs—and so much more! Schedule a Career Counseling Session Discover Our Career Services Explore a range of Career Design and Development services tailored to support undergraduate students, graduate students, adult and continuing education learners, and alumni in achieving their career goals and professional growth. Career Design and Development will have walk-in career support, Fridays from 1-3 pm in the CDD Lounge. Undergraduate Click to Open Our Career Design and Development services are designed to equip full-time and part-time undergraduate students with the tools and guidance needed to transition smoothly from academia to the professional world. During your time at Widener you will have access to: Personalized Career Counseling : One-on-one sessions with career counselors to explore interests, values, and goals, and create a strategic plan for career aspirations. Resume and Cover Letter Workshops : Workshops to enhance your application materials, focusing on crafting compelling documents that highlight your strengths. Mock Interviews : Sessions to build confidence and refine interview skills, including constructive feedback to improve performance. Job Search Assistance : Resources and strategies to navigate the job market, including tools and tips for finding and applying for opportunities. Networking Events and Career Fairs : Opportunities to connect with industry professionals and potential employers, expanding your network and exploring job prospects. Graduate Click to Open Students Enrolled in Full-Time, Cohort-Based Programs (e.g., Physical Therapy (DPT), Clinical Psychology (Psy.D)) or Part-Time Graduate Study Programs (Main Campus): Counselor Appointments : Schedule appointments based on availability, conducted via phone, Zoom, or in person. Career Events : Participate in on-campus Career Design and Development clinics, workshops, and career fairs. Online Resources : Access various online resources available on the University’s website. Early-Evening Office Hours : Attend twice a month, either remotely or in person, for added convenience. Students Enrolled in Entirely Online Degree Programs: Online Resources : Have unlimited access to online resources on the University’s website for career design and development support without the need for in-person attendance. Adult & Continuing Studies Click to Open Students enrolled in a Continuing Studies program on the University’s Main Campus with a minimum of 3 credits per semester have access to the following career services: Counselor Appointments : Schedule individual appointments based on availability, either by phone, Zoom, or in person, with a minimum of 3 credits per semester. Career Events : Attend all on-campus Career Design and Development clinics, workshops, and career fairs. Online Resources : Utilize the online resources available on this website. Alumni Click to Open As a valued member of the Widener University community, you continue to have access to career guidance even after graduation. Whether you need help with job search strategies, updating your resume, or making a strategic career transition, the Office of Career Design and Development is here to support you. As an alumnus, you can: Participate in Events : Join professional skills workshops, employer information sessions, and career fairs hosted by Career Design and Development. Access Online Resources : Use the University’s website for 24/7 access to career resources. For those who have graduated within the past 24 months: Enjoy Full Services : Access the same services as current students, including one-on-one in-person or virtual appointments with a career counselor and access to Handshake, Widener’s online job site. For alumni who graduated more than 24 months ago: Consultation Services : Receive up to two one-hour consultations, either in-person or via phone/Zoom, including resume and cover letter reviews and guidance on LinkedIn and other career platforms. If you need assistance with your Handshake account, please contact Career Design and Development at careers@widener.edu . Upcoming Events October 5 • 02:00 PM Civil & Construction Management Career Fair Build Connections. Shape Your Future. Step into opportunity at the Civil Engineering & Construction September 16 • 02:00 PM School of Business Administration Career Fair October 12 • 10:00 AM Mock Madness: Resume Feedback and Interview Skills Workshop (10/12-10/15) November 5 • 12:00 PM Federal Jobs Workshop Success Blog Career Fair 101: How to Prepare, Network, & Follow Up Career fairs are a chance to explore your options and practice connecting with employers. This guide shows you how to prepare ahead of time, manage conversations during the event, and follow up afterward so you leave feeling more confident and prepared. Learning to Advocate for Yourself in College College is an exciting time full of new challenges and opportunities. But with all the independence that comes with college life, it can sometimes feel overwhelming to handle everything on your own. That's where self-advocacy comes in! Finding the Right Campus Job for You A campus job at Widener gives you hands-on experience, new connections, and flexible opportunities. Whether you qualify for work study or not, there are plenty of ways to find the right fit for you. View More Blogs Quick Links Find Campus Jobs & Internships on Handshake Use AI to Polish Your Personal Branding on Jobscan Prepare to Ace Your Interview Network with Alumni on WidenerCONNECT Say Hello to the Career Design & Development Team Where We're Located 526 E. 14th Street Hours of Operation The office is open for all students Monday through Friday 9 am-5 pm. Extended hours are available for Graduate and Continuing Studies Students Wednesdays and Thursdays from 4 pm-7 pm. Follow Us on Social Media Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Student Perspectives You can take what you learned in the classroom and then apply that to the real world. If we're going over a lecture and we're talking about framing and then we go out to a job and they're doing metal or wood framing, you can see how. Semaj Smith-Barber Class of 2028 Undergraduate | Construction Management Read Semaj's Story Student Perspectives As a former Marine, it helps that Widener is a Yellow Ribbon school--whatever the GI Bill doesn't cover Widener will forgive. I plan to get my bachelor’s, work in a hospital, then I can get into flight nursing and practice trauma care. Samuel Flood Class of 2027 Undergraduate | Bachelor of science in nursing Read Samuel's Story Student Perspectives Camp has always been such a big part of my life... I think the education I got through Widener really helped me to fuel that passion and helped me to make connections that I didn’t know could have been made. Sophia Hastings Class of 2018 Undergraduate | Social Work; Gender, Women & Sexuality Studies Read Sophia's Story Student Perspectives Working at Widener's Community Nursing Clinic is a really unique experience that a lot of schools don't have to offer. It’s real life scenarios where we are able to relate to it cause it's around us. Taylor Wise Class of 2025 Undergraduate | Bachelor of science in nursing Read Taylor's Story Student Perspectives Performing Gameday Satisfaction Market Research for the Philadelphia Union was unforgettable. We got an in-depth look at fan, stadium worker, and media reporter insights on the Philadelphia Union, Subaru Park, and loyal fanbase. The energy was palpable. Ahmad Kamara Class of 2024 Student Perspectives I loved having the opportunity to do research, but also having the opportunity to research with a large medical device company—that’s something you don’t see quite often. Shaylyn Westmoreland Class of 2023 and 2024 Graduate | Biomedical Engineering Read Shaylyn's Story Get in Touch Meet the Team Resources for Faculty Resources for Employers Career Design & Development 526 E. 14th Street 610-499-4176 careers@widener.edu Widener Career Design & Development Facebook Widener Career Design & Development X Widener Career Design & Development Instagram Janet R. Long Associate Vice President, Career Design & Development Office of Career Design and Development 526 E. 14th Street (610) 499-4045 jrlong@widener.edu Julie Abrams Director of Professional Development, Career Design & Development 526 E.14th St. 610-499-1271 jabrams@widener.edu mySuccess Widener University 1 University Place Chester, PA 19013 610-499-1266 studentsuccess@widener.edu Join Widener on Social Media Widener University Facebook Widener University Instagram Widener University Twitter Widener University TikTok Widener University LinkedIn 2026 Widener University Campus Safety Report It Privacy Consumer Information"
